        "nyc-zr:23-21",
        "nyc-zr:114-02",
        "nyc-zr:66-11"
      ],
      "finding": "No blanket 5,000-square-foot rule: the first R1-R5 route also requires transit geography and frontage and excludes R1/R2; other community-facility/senior-housing routes exist. Section 114-02 excludes Bay Ridge lots existing December 5, 2024 above five acres. Section 23-21 markup confirms 0.75 with superscript footnote 1, not 0.751; qualifying R3-2 sites have 1.00. Footnote 1 caps a single dwelling's equivalent FAR at 0.60 on standard lots of at least 4,000 sq ft. Definition found at character 174905 in a 273324-character section. August 12 cutoff finds nothing; August 13 succeeds, not evidence of enactment on that date.",
      "omissions": [
        "No parcel/transit-boundary determination, HPD regulatory-agreement analysis, or complete special-district survey.",
        "12-10 contains 17 source-media descriptors; unacquired media not interpreted.",
        "Two listed 12-10 versions share one artifact/snapshot: parser projections, not two historical laws."
      ]
