      "finding": "18VAC50-22-40 requires a qualified individual age 18+, one year of relevant experience, full-time employment/responsible-management status, specialty prerequisites, disclosures and a management business course. Section -61's HTML row pairs ELE with a master electrician tradesman license and No in its board-approved-examination column; it does not waive the separate master license. Section 54.1-1100 contains Class A/B/C value alternatives; its C wording is single project over $1,000 but under $30,000 OR annual value under $250,000. No final class assignment is made. Section 54.1-1101(A)(15)'s $25,000 subcontract-work exemption preserves individual-license requirements.",
